# Login Implementation Walkthrough

I have successfully implemented the login flow using Google Sheets as the backend for credential verification.

## Changes Made

### Backend
- **New API Endpoint**: [src/pages/api/login.ts](file:///Users/jesus.traslavina/Desktop/XPO/gemini/bartimeo/bartimeo-app/src/pages/api/login.ts)
  - Verifies credentials against `userticket` Google Sheet (Columns A & B).
  - Returns 200 OK on success, 401 Unauthorized on failure.
- **Load Testing Endpoint**: [src/pages/api/test-write.ts](file:///Users/jesus.traslavina/Desktop/XPO/gemini/bartimeo/bartimeo-app/src/pages/api/test-write.ts)
  - Writes data to `test` sheet for validating write performance.

### Frontend
- **New Component**: [src/components/LoginModule.tsx](file:///Users/jesus.traslavina/Desktop/XPO/gemini/bartimeo/bartimeo-app/src/components/LoginModule.tsx)
  - React component managing the login form, API calls, and local storage state.
  - Handles "Ingresar" and "Salir" states.
  - Shows a modal with backdrop blur for login inputs.
- **Updated Header**: [src/components/home/HomeHeader.astro](file:///Users/jesus.traslavina/Desktop/XPO/gemini/bartimeo/bartimeo-app/src/components/home/HomeHeader.astro)
  - Replaced the static "Ingresar" button with the dynamic [LoginModule](file:///Users/jesus.traslavina/Desktop/XPO/gemini/bartimeo/bartimeo-app/src/components/LoginModule.tsx#5-190) component.
- **Integration**: [src/pages/index.astro](file:///Users/jesus.traslavina/Desktop/XPO/gemini/bartimeo/bartimeo-app/src/pages/index.astro) and Components
  - Existing logic in [index.astro](file:///Users/jesus.traslavina/Desktop/XPO/gemini/bartimeo/bartimeo-app/src/pages/index.astro) checks `localStorage` and removes `blur-md` classes from locked content.
  - Validated that `LoginOverlay` component correctly applies these classes.

## Verification Results

### Automated Browser Verification
I ran a browser subagent to verify the end-to-end flow:
1.  **Login**: Successfully logged in with test credentials (`3123415728` / `CZ50`).
2.  **Unlock**: Confirmed that "Ranking General" and other sections unlocked (blur removed).
3.  **Logout**: Confirmed "Salir" button works and re-locks the content.

### Load Testing
I executed a load test with 1000 requests:
- **Login (Read)**: Started seeing `429 Too Many Requests` (Quota Exceeded) errors from Google Sheets API after several hundred requests.
- **Write**: Similarly limited by the Google Sheets quota "Read requests per minute per user" and "Write requests per minute".
- **Conclusion**: For high-traffic scenarios (1000 concurrent users), directly hitting Google Sheets is not scalable without caching (e.g., Redis) or a database. For the "retry" scope of 3000 users, it might be fine if traffic is spread out, but burst traffic will hit limits.

